blurb = "The text explains that the butterbur in Akita grew to an extraordinary height of one jō (about 3 meters), and the leaves were the size of an umbrella. It claims that the hole in the stalks could fit three herrings. Both the stalk and flower were edible, but the taste was inferior to the smaller varieties."
